// SimCam — local signing override template.
//
// Copy this file to "SimCamSigning.local.xcconfig" (in the same directory),
// fill in your team id + cert SHA-1, then re-run `xcodegen generate`.
//
// The .local.xcconfig file is gitignored. The template (this file) is
// committed so newcomers know what to do.
//
// To find your team id and certificate SHA-1:
//
//   $ security find-identity -v -p codesigning
//   1) <SHA-1>  "Apple Development: <your email> (<TEAM_ID>)"
//
// The 40-char hex string before the quoted name is the SHA-1.
// The 10-char string in parentheses inside the quoted name is the team id.
//
// We pin by SHA-1 (not by the display name "Apple Development") because
// xcodebuild on recent Xcode versions remaps "Apple Development" to
// "Mac Development" for macOS targets, and Personal Team accounts only have a
// single universal "Apple Development" cert. Using the SHA-1 sidesteps that
// mapping and signs the build with your existing identity.

// SIMCAM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM   = ABCDE12345
// SIMCAM_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567
// SIMCAM_CODE_SIGN_STYLE    = Manual

